# (15k masked pixels) peaked at 10.2 GiB MaxRSS; batch 0's sacct MaxRSS replaces this
# (next 16/32/64 GB step >= 1.5x the peak) before batch 1.
# One cell per array task on `ral` (CPU work never goes on `gpu`). numba cells pin their
# BLAS threads to 1 (production per-worker cost); JAX CPU cells get NPROC=8.
#
# BATCH 0 = TIMING ARM (decision D9). It runs every group leg: group bounds
# multi_galaxy (1.6x the masked pixels, two dPIE extra galaxies). Each leg's wall lands
# in output/p2d_logs/walls.tsv; batch 1's WALL-BASIS rows will cite them
# (source: measured-wall) and its --time / --mem are set from them.
#
# WALL-BASIS: nothing measured yet; 3600 s per leg is a declared guess
# (3x floor), ~10x the imaging hst legs of the nearest measured size.
#   3 leg(s): delaunay jax_cpu_sparse_fp64 breakdown, mge jax_cpu_dense_fp64 breakdown, rectangular jax_cpu_sparse_fp64 breakdown
#   cell: group/likelihood_breakdown/euclid  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: unmeasured  probe-first: yes  wall: 3600  headroom: 3.0
#   2 leg(s): delaunay numba_cpu_sparse_fp64 breakdown, rectangular numba_cpu_sparse_fp64 breakdown
#   cell: group/likelihood_breakdown_numba/euclid  device: ral_cpu  precision: fp64
#   source: unmeasured  probe-first: yes  wall: 3600  headroom: 3.0
#   3 leg(s): delaunay jax_cpu_sparse_fp64 runtime, mge jax_cpu_dense_fp64 runtime, rectangular jax_cpu_sparse_fp64 runtime
